	"metadata":{"version":"1.0-1.0"},
	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"2fccba2e6b3b7288",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Discrete-Time",
			"type":"text",
			"x":760,
			"y":-923,
			"width":300,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"e60a142db4d6d8b0",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Continous-Time",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1654,
			"y":-923,
			"width":322,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"57bdc9d73618bf8b",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Finite Horizon",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-761,
			"width":330,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"12df75f758e79959",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"$$\nJ = \\int_0^T x(t)^\\top Q(t) x(t) + u(t)^\\top R(t) u(t) dt + x(T)^\\top P_f x(T)\n$$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-701,
			"width":530,
			"height":106,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"9a726867de1b05f7",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$0 = Q + A^\\top P_\\infty + P_\\infty A - P_\\infty B R^{-1}B^\\top P_\\infty$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-67,
			"width":570,
			"height":90,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"b5fd08057d967557",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Infinite Horizon",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":146,
			"width":287,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"31754a067902c2bc",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"Useful for “**persistent**” tracking and regulation problems",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1266,
			"y":146,
			"width":554,
			"height":60,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"632b9947f8d286cb",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"$$\nJ = \\sum_{i=k}^\\infty \\gamma^{i-k} \\left(x_i^\\top Q x_i + u_i^\\top R u_i\\right)\n$$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":206,
			"width":521,
			"height":103,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"375c37672a4d63c6",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Discrete-Time Algebraic Riccati Equation (DARE)",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":309,
			"width":521,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"ef9928f22c02dd52",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Time-invariant Control Law",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1500,
			"y":309,
			"width":320,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"4d5a7af6f6d0454e",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$u(k) = K_\\infty x(k)$\n$K_\\infty = - \\gamma (B^\\top P_\\infty B+R)^{-1} B^\\top P_\\infty A$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1500,
			"y":359,
			"width":320,
			"height":100,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"0fa812e1e892bc68",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Continuous-Time Algebraic Riccati Equation (CARE)",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-118,
			"width":570,
			"height":51
		},
		{
			"id":"ed82c8a7aedc89d8",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"$$\nJ = \\sum_{i=k}^{N-1} \\gamma^{i-k} \\left(x(i)^\\top Q x(i) + u(i)^\\top R u(i)\\right) + x(N)^\\top P_f x(N)\n$$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":-700,
			"width":440,
			"height":110,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"b26511f485edb7ac",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":" Derive the optimal control law using **Dynamic Programming** / **Bellman Recursion** / **backward recursion** from end time $N$.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1266,
			"y":-780,
			"width":534,
			"height":80,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"0fcf31d67be8361f",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"$$\nJ = \\int_0^\\infty x(t)^\\top Q x(t) + u(t)^\\top R u(t) dt\n$$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-220,
			"width":570,
			"height":102,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"6c62c9be9eca6278",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"Similar to **Finite Horizon**, but with terminal cost $P_f = 0$ ",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1920,
			"y":153,
			"width":282,
			"height":77,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"00d8cf63d1fd2175",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# LQ Control",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-159,
			"y":-1436,
			"width":322,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"6fed1101777cce22",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Infinite Horizon",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-280,
			"width":330,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"ed2986f6ce8ed0bc",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Value Function",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1500,
			"y":459,
			"width":320,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"d8b8355f139d00dc",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$V(x(k)) = x(k)^\\top P_\\infty x(k)$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1500,
			"y":509,
			"width":320,
			"height":74,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"a4ae83cc9b621016",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":">[!steps] Steps\n>Either solve DARE directly, or\n>1. Initialize the backward recursion with the Riccati matrix $P_{0} = 0$\n>2. Iteratively compute the Riccati matrix for $i \\to \\infty$ until convergence via $$ P_{i+1} = Q + A^\\top P_i A - (A^\\top P_i B) (B^\\top P_i B+R)^{-1} (B^\\top P_i A) $$\n>3. The optimal feedback gain is obtained as $$ K_\\infty = -(B^\\top P_\\infty B+R)^{-1} B^\\top P_\\infty A $$\n\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":583,
			"width":841,
			"height":338
		},
		{
			"id":"8f5b19d99146f070",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"#### Sources\n- [Wikipedia: Linear-quadratic regulator](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear%E2%80%93quadratic_regulator)\n- [What Is Linear Quadratic Regulator (LQR) Optimal Control?](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E_RDCFOlJx4&ab_channel=MATLAB)\n- [CS 285: Lecture 10, Part 3](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gqTE8-tH3Iw&list=PL_iWQOsE6TfVYGEGiAOMaOzzv41Jfm_Ps&index=43&ab_channel=RAIL)\n- [Underactuated Robotics, Russ Tedrake, Chapter 8 Linear Quadratic Regulator](https://underactuated.mit.edu/lqr.html)",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1531,
			"y":-1296,
			"width":642,
			"height":183
		},
		{
			"id":"529087a943fa4c76",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Finite Horizon",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":-761,
			"width":287,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"d74bffe673c7b1c4",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Time-variant Control Law",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-900,
			"y":-701,
			"width":318,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"bdbd21c07535819e",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$u(t) = K(t)x(t)$\n$K(t) = -R^{-1}B^\\top P(t)$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-900,
			"y":-651,
			"width":318,
			"height":100,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"fb10fb501d33cc25",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Value Function",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-900,
			"y":-551,
			"width":318,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"eb397f3209e2b45a",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$V(x(t)) = x(t)^\\top P(t) x(t)$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-900,
			"y":-501,
			"width":318,
			"height":100,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"4ca8afc2c8d1ff7d",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"Design an **optimal** state-feedback controller for\n- **linear time-invariant** systems\n- **quadratic** cost function\n\nThe weights $Q$ and $R$ allow for a trade-off between how well the controller drives the system error to zero versus with how much effort.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":280,
			"y":-1505,
			"width":618,
			"height":199,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"07c321b015ba608f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Note:** The LQR solution is **independent** of the **noise variance**! However, the performance gets worse with higher variance.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-1575,
			"width":618,
			"height":70
		},
		{
			"id":"f00863df8097c4c1",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Differential Riccati Equation (DRE)",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-595,
			"width":530,
			"height":51
		},
		{
			"id":"cd0ff0ac9530baa5",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$-\\dot{P}(t) = Q(t) + A(t)^\\top P(t) + P(t) A(t) - P(t) B(t) R(t)^{-1} B(t)^\\top P(t)$\n$P(t_f) = P_f$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-546,
			"width":530,
			"height":145,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"193e1d37140c89ef",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Note:** CARE is DRE for a time-invariant Riccati matrix, i.e., $\\dot{P}(t) = 0$.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2184,
			"y":-280,
			"width":530,
			"height":60,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"72979f94546e26be",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$P = Q + \\gamma A^\\top P A - \\gamma^2 (A^\\top PB)(\\gamma B^\\top P B + R)^{-1}(B^\\top PA)$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":359,
			"width":521,
			"height":60,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"0eb318bb6d547b93",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"**Note:** Under common assumptions, $P_\\infty$ is the fixed-point solution of the DARE and can thus be computed by arbitrary initialization of $P_0$ (often $0$) and iterative application of the **RDE** until convergence to the **positive-definite** solution of$$P_{i+1} = Q + \\gamma A^\\top P_i A - \\gamma^2 (A^\\top P_i B)(\\gamma B^\\top P_i B + R)^{-1}(B^\\top P_i A)$$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":419,
			"width":521,
			"height":164
		},
		{
			"id":"7f50ff3450d0c160",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"**Note:** The LQR is a special form of $H_2$ control.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-656,
			"y":-1436,
			"width":369,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"64b8d28a0f2fa7d8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Note:** There also exists a \"square-root form\" of the DRE which ensures better numerical stability when being solved.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1430,
			"y":-401,
			"width":530,
			"height":61
		},
		{
			"id":"981a4dc60be46cfe",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Time-invariant Control Law",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-860,
			"y":-117,
			"width":320,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"98ec93edaf55c949",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$u(t) = K_\\infty x(t)$\n$K_\\infty = -R^{-1}B^\\top P_\\infty$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-860,
			"y":-67,
			"width":320,
			"height":90,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"d29962669e2f6c37",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Value Function",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-860,
			"y":23,
			"width":320,
			"height":50
		},
		{
			"id":"a84c5b0842811ece",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$V(x(t)) = x(t)^\\top P_\\infty x(t)$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-860,
			"y":73,
			"width":320,
			"height":80,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"45afc0e1837e3433",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"The value function represents the **cost-to-go**, so optimal actions will move down this landscape **as quickly as possible**. Here, $-P_\\infty x$ is the direction of steepest descent of the value function $V(x) = x^\\top P_\\infty x$. However, not all directions are possible to achieve in state space (since we can only use $u$ to change $x$), so we need to project this descent into the action space as $-B^\\top P_\\infty x$. Finally, we placed weightings on the actions with the matrix $R$, which biases the direction of descent into the lowest cost direction as $R^{-1}B^\\top P_\\infty$, resulting in the optimal gain $K$.\n\nNote that the value function $V(x)$ directly encodes the long-term dynamics and costs.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-1136,
			"y":208,
			"width":873,
			"height":202,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"0e1fd2322e9c1dc9",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"**Note:** The ARE has a **unique** positive-definite solution **if and only if** the system is **controllable**.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-84,
			"y":48,
			"width":507,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"cd225a7ea0f08ac5",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Time-variant Control Law",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1419,
			"y":-700,
			"width":381,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"98db4a5661a56b8e",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$u(k) = K(k) x(k)$\n$K(k)=-(B^\\top P(k+1) B + R)^{-1} B^\\top P(k+1) A$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1419,
			"y":-640,
			"width":381,
			"height":110,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"0129f44ac201957a",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Riccati Difference Equation (RDE)",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":-590,
			"width":440,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"62f6e2336cce61f1",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$P(k) = Q + A^\\top P(k+1) A - (A^\\top P(k+1) B) (B^\\top P(k+1) B + R)^{-1} (B^\\top P(k+1) A)$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":-530,
			"width":639,
			"height":60,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"07e6a551f4c8f5c7",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"$V(x(k)) = x(k)^\\top P(k) x(k)$\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1800,
			"y":-641,
			"width":381,
			"height":80,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"3aeb1200c5e232d5",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"### Value Function",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1800,
			"y":-700,
			"width":381,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ca93f2a3300815aa",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"text":"# Finite Horizon\n**Objective function:**$$J(x_0) = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\gamma^{k} \\left(\\frac{1}{2} x_k^\\top Q_k x_k + \\frac{1}{2} u_k^\\top R_k u_k + u_k^\\top N_k x_k\\right) + \\frac{1}{2} x_N^\\top P_f x_N$$\n**Resulting Riccati Equation:**$$P_k = Q_k + A_k^\\top P_{k+1} A_k - (N_k^\\top + A_k^\\top P_{k+1} B_k)(B_k^\\top P_{k+1} B_k + R_k)^{-1}(N_k + B_k^\\top P_{k+1} A_k)$$\n**Optimal control gain:**$$K_k = -(B_k^\\top P_{k+1} B_k + R_k)^{-1} (B_k^\\top P_{k+1} A_k + N_k)$$\n# Infinite Horizon\n**Objective function:**$$J(x_0) = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\gamma^{k} \\left(\\frac{1}{2} x_k^\\top Q x_k + \\frac{1}{2} u_k^\\top R u_k + u_k^\\top N x_k\\right)$$\n**Resulting Riccati Equation:**$$P_\\infty = Q + A^\\top P_\\infty A - (N^\\top + A^\\top P_\\infty B)(B^\\top P_\\infty B + R)^{-1}(P+B^\\top P_\\infty A)$$\n**Optimal control gain:**$$K_\\infty=-(B^\\top P_\\infty B+R)^{-1} (B^\\top P_\\infty A + N)$$\n$$u(k) = K_\\infty x(k)$$\nSource: [https://underactuated.mit.edu/lqr.html](https://underactuated.mit.edu/lqr.html)",
			"type":"text",
			"x":2480,
			"y":-1005,
			"width":660,
			"height":725
		},
		{
			"id":"b1b8004f3386a829",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The LQR cost can be rewritten as$$J(K) = \\mathbb{E}_{x_0 \\sim \\mathcal{D}} \\left[ \\sum_{t=0}^{\\infty} x_0^\\top \\big( (A - BK)^\\top \\big)^t \\, (Q + K^\\top R K) \\, (A - BK)^t x_0 \\right],$$which is a function of $K$. This cost can also be expressed as$$J(K) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\!\\left( P_K \\Sigma_0 \\right),$$where $\\Sigma_0 = \\mathbb{E}[x_0 x_0^\\top]$ is the (full-rank) covariance matrix of the initial state $x_0$​, and $P_K$​ is the solution to the following **Lyapunov equation**:$$(A - BK)^\\top P_K (A - BK) + Q + K^\\top R K = P_K.$$",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-112,
			"y":-526,
			"width":563,
			"height":292
		},
		{
			"id":"96d0feaee7678677",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"$Q$: symmetric positive (semi-)definite\n$R$: symmetric positive definite\n$N$: symmetric positive definite (?)\n$\\gamma$: discount factor",
			"type":"text",
			"x":982,
			"y":-1463,
			"width":374,
			"height":115
		},
		{
			"id":"426e259e32a2daec",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"If $Q$ (only) positive semi-definite, then $(A,Q^{\\frac{1}{2}})$ **needs to be observable**, which guarantees that unstable states are (indirectly) observable via the cost.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":1451,
			"y":-1446,
			"width":591,
			"height":80,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"6d8cdb5cc40edfb1",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"The terminal cost $P_f$ is **symmetric** and **positive definite**.\n\n> [!proof]- Derivation\n> We want to minimize the cost function\n> ![[Pasted image 20240626145331.png]]\n> ![[Pasted image 20240626145528.png]]\n> ![[Pasted image 20240626145626.png]]\n> ![[Pasted image 20240626145747.png]]\n> ![[Pasted image 20240626145903.png]]\n> ![[Pasted image 20240626150041.png]]\n\n\n\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-224,
			"y":-793,
			"width":452,
			"height":124,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"3cb78b07bea8daa8",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"**Note:** The **Riccati Equation** gives the **optimal** solution and optimal cost-to-go, while the **Lyapunov equation** just gives the corresponding cost-to-go for a stabilizing policy (which is not necessarily the optimal one).",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-112,
			"y":-234,
			"width":563,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"0d14b2609d29f9e7",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":">[!steps] Steps\n>1. Initialize the backward recursion with the terminal cost $P(N) = P_f$\n>2. For each backward step, compute the Riccati matrix ...\n>\t1. ... directly as $$ P(k) = Q + A^\\top P(k+1) A - (A^\\top P(k+1) B) (B^\\top P(k+1) B + R)^{-1} (B^\\top P(k+1) A) $$\n>\t2. ... or together with the feedback gain as $$P(k) = Q + A^\\top P(k+1) A + K(k)^\\top B^\\top P(k+1) A$$ and $$ K(k) = -(B^\\top P(k+1) B + R)^{-1} B^\\top P(k+1) A$$\n \nThis yields the **optimal cost-to-go** as $J^*_{0\\to N} = x(0)^\\top P(0) x(0)$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":979,
			"y":-470,
			"width":821,
			"height":433
		},
		{
			"id":"bedd1b33b66b3e09",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"text":"# Finite Horizon\n$$\nJ = \\int_0^T x(t)^\\top Q x(t) + u(t)^\\top R u(t) + x(t)^\\top N u(t) dt + x(T)^\\top P_f x(T)\n$$\n$$u(t) = K(t)x(t)$$\n$$K(t) = -R^{-1} (B^\\top P(t) + N)$$\n# Infinite Horizon\n$$\nJ = \\int_0^\\infty x(t)^\\top Q x(t) + u(t)^\\top R u(t) + x(t)^\\top N u(t) dt\n$$\n$$u(t) = K_\\infty x(t)$$\n$$K_\\infty = -R^{-1} (B^\\top P_\\infty + N)$$\nwith ARE\n$$\nA^\\top P_\\infty + P_\\infty A - (P_\\infty B + N) R^{-1} (B^\\top P_\\infty + N^\\top) + Q = 0\n$$",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-2680,
			"y":-923,
			"width":660,
			"height":474
		},
		{
			"id":"2967a8da0fd2b2cd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Note:** LQR can also be solved using Convex Optimization and [[Linear Matrix Inequality (LMI)|LMIs]], instead of using the Riccati Equation.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-1645,
			"width":618,
			"height":70
		},
		{
			"id":"2da648f634165b9b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Performance Signal $z_k$\n![[lqr_block_diagram.png|center|300]]\nThe cost function is a summation of individual cost terms over $N$ time steps$$J = \\sum_{k=0}^{N} c(x_k,u_k)$$where we can also define each individual cost term as a \"performance signal\" $z_t$. For the standard quadratic cost function of the LQR, we can rewrite the cost as$$J = \\sum_{k=0}^{N} z_k^\\top z_k$$where we define$$z_k = \\begin{bmatrix} Q^{\\frac{1}{2}} & 0\\\\ 0 & R^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\\\ \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} x_k\\\\ u_k\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}.$$The performance signal $z_k$ can be seen as an \"virtual\" output of the system, which directly motivates the **detectability condition** of $(A,Q^{\\frac{1}{2}})$, ensuring that a diverging state can be seen in the \"virtual\" cost output.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-142,
			"y":459,
			"width":623,
			"height":691,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"88958a22ce4e1fcd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Note:** The OCP is **non-convex** (bilinear?) in the control gains $K(k)$.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-254,
			"y":-1193,
			"width":524,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"abbda266550be0f7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"In LQ Control, we want to solve the following problem:$$\\begin{align}\n\\min_{u(k)} \\;\\;& \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} x(k)^\\top Q x(k) + u(k)^\\top R u(k) + x(N)^\\top P_f x(N)\\\\\n\\text{s.t.} \\;\\;& x(k+1) = A x(k) + B u(k), \\; \\forall k = 0,...,N-1\\\\\n& u(k) = K(k) x(k), \\; \\forall k = 0,...,N-1\\\\\n& x(0) = x_0.\\\\\n\\end{align}$$",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-254,
			"y":-1376,
			"width":524,
			"height":183,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"6930171e9963091d",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"**Note:** For a discrete-time, infinite-horizon, linear quadratic optimal control problem, if $(A, B)$ is **stabilizable**, then there exists an input sequence that yields a finite cost. If, in addition, $(A, Q^{\\frac{1}{2}})$ is **detectable**, then there exists a **unique** solution to the DARE. The detectability condition ensures that the cost can only be finite if the state is finite.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":-142,
			"y":206,
			"width":623,
			"height":145,
			"color":"2"
		}
	]
}